---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy — KeeForge" description="KeeForge does not collect your vault data. The only information we ever see is what you choose to send us through the in-app feedback form.">
    <div class="privacy">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to KeeForge</a>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: April 2026</p>

        <div class="content">
            <p class="lead">KeeForge does not collect your vault data. The only information we ever see is what you choose to send us through the in-app feedback form.</p>

            <h2>No Analytics</h2>
            <p>KeeForge contains no analytics frameworks, no crash reporting SDKs, and no usage tracking of any kind.</p>

            <h2>No Telemetry</h2>
            <p>KeeForge does not make background network requests. The only outbound connections the app ever makes are: (1) to the cloud storage providers you explicitly configure (iCloud Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, etc.) to sync your database files, and (2) a single request to our feedback endpoint when <em>you</em> tap &ldquo;Send&rdquo; in the in-app feedback form (see below).</p>

            <h2>No Accounts</h2>
            <p>KeeForge does not require or offer account creation. There is nothing to sign up for.</p>

            <h2>Your Vault Data</h2>
            <p>Your passwords, entries, attachments, and master password stay on your device and in your own cloud storage. KeeForge has no ability to read, access, or transmit your vault data to anyone. The app operates entirely offline except for the file syncing you choose to enable and the opt-in feedback submissions described below.</p>

            <h2>Feedback Submissions</h2>
            <p>KeeForge includes an in-app feedback form (available from Settings and from certain error screens). The form is entirely optional &mdash; the app's features and services do not depend on using it. When, and only when, you tap &ldquo;Send,&rdquo; the app submits the following information to our feedback endpoint at <code>https://feedback.keeforge.com/api/feedback</code> over HTTPS:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>The free-text message you typed.</li>
                <li>If you were sending feedback from an error screen: the error code, error category, and a short technical description of the error. These contain no entries, passwords, file contents, or file paths from your vault.</li>
                <li>Basic diagnostic information about your device and app build: the app version, build number, iOS version, and device model (for example, <code>iPhone16,2</code>).</li>
                <li>Whether you opted in to follow-up contact, and, <em>only if you opted in</em>, the contact address (typically an email) you entered. If you do not tick the follow-up box, no contact information is transmitted.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We use this information solely to read and respond to your feedback and to diagnose bugs. We do not use it for advertising, profiling, or analytics, and we do not sell it. Submissions are stored on infrastructure operated on our behalf by our hosting provider; any such provider is contractually required to protect the data to the same standard described in this policy and to process it only on our instructions.</p>
            <p>We retain feedback submissions for up to 24 months so we can follow up on related reports, and then delete them. You can withdraw consent for follow-up, or request deletion of a feedback submission and any associated contact information, at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@keeforge.com">support@keeforge.com</a> from the address you submitted, or by opening an issue on <a href="https://github.com/crazytan/KeeForge">GitHub</a>. You can also simply decline to use the feedback form &mdash; if you never tap &ldquo;Send,&rdquo; nothing is transmitted.</p>

            <h2>Children</h2>
            <p>KeeForge is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect information from children through the feedback form.</p>

            <h2>Open Source</h2>
            <p>Don't take our word for it. KeeForge is open source under the GPLv3 license. You can <a href="https://github.com/crazytan/KeeForge">audit the code yourself</a>, including the exact fields the feedback form sends.</p>

            <h2>Changes To This Policy</h2>
            <p>If we change what the app collects or how we use it, we will update this page and change the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above before the change ships in a public build.</p>

            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>If you have questions about this policy, email <a href="mailto:support@keeforge.com">support@keeforge.com</a> or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/crazytan/KeeForge">GitHub</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Base>

<style>
    .privacy {
        max-width: 640px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 60px 24px 80px;
    }

    .back-link {
        display: inline-block;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--text-dim);
        margin-bottom: 40px;
        transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover {
        color: var(--text);
    }

    h1 {
        font-size: 2.4rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        background: none;
        -webkit-text-fill-color: var(--text);
    }

    .updated {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: var(--text-dim);
        margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .content {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 24px;
    }

    .lead {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--green);
        padding-bottom: 24px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    h2 {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: -16px;
    }

    p {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--text-dim);
    }

    @media (max-width: 480px) {
        .privacy {
            padding: 40px 20px 60px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 1.8rem;
        }
    }
</style>
